  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "7fa74a92-1b64-b238-3b40-10e371f7a97e",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "64c23cfa-f376-2bfd-2e93-e11941db619b",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The content of the course was based on common encounters AKU drivers are likely to experience with passengers in a typical working day. The principal objective was to develop the learners' confidence with using English in common work-related contexts. With each module, the drivers learned situational language for these encounters, focusing on vocabulary and functional phrases.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "By the end of the course, the drivers reported that they felt far more confident when using English for greeting passengers and engaging in conversations with them. They also felt that they were able to deal better with queries about places to visit in Karachi.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
